    "reference_policy": "Reuse independent Q1 sources; only missing/unclear/conflicting items may be supplemented. Preserve originals and revisions uniformly across all methods.",
    "reference_input_isolation": "DEV evaluation reference never enters local prompt, graph, candidates, checker acceptance policy, or final generation. DEV local classification labels used only for validation/evaluation, not gradients.",
    "claim_split_rule": "A substantive judgement is one independently assessable proposition about a fact/object/event/status/stage, a rule/scope/exception, an application, or a conclusion. Split only when clauses can have different truth or support values. Merge repetitions and paraphrases of the same proposition, across fields. Do not count citations, headings, stylistic remarks, or every word as claims. An explicitly qualified uncertainty or assumption is assessed in its stated scope. Distinguish an asserted fact from an attributed claim. Alternative accounts of the same issue remain different claims when their speakers, objects, stage, or asserted content differ.",
